## 19. Final MVP Acceptance Criteria

VibeGuard is ready for hackathon demonstration when:

1. The application launches successfully.
2. A user can upload a supported source-code archive.
3. The scanner executes real security checks.
4. Findings include evidence and remediation guidance.
5. The controlled vulnerable authorization test fails as expected.
6. The corrected authorization test passes.
7. Verification results are based on executed checks.
8. A report can be downloaded.
9. The interface works on desktop and mobile.
10. Tests, limitations, and setup instructions are documented.

## 20. Conclusion

VibeGuard aims to bridge the gap between fast AI-assisted development and responsible application security. By combining deterministic security checks, an understandable findings interface, controlled authorization testing, and repeatable fix verification, the MVP demonstrates a practical way to help beginner developers identify and address common security risks before deployment.

The Indiathon version will focus on a small, functional, demonstrable workflow. Its success will be evaluated through actual test results and usability rather than unsupported claims that an application is completely secure.